<title>Memory configuration</title>
<body>
<p>The system provides eight onboard memory slots for installing supported
memory modules.</p>
<p><image align="center" href="up5g2_memorylocation.jpg" placement="break"><alt>Memory slots</alt></image><table colsep="1" frame="topbot" pgwide="1" rowheader="firstcol" rowsep="1">
<tgroup cols="2"><colspec colname="col1" colwidth="29.95*"/><colspec colname="col2" colwidth="70.05*"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="top">Item</entry>
<entry valign="top">Description</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry>Slots</entry>
<entry>8 memory slots across 4 channels</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>Memory type</entry>
<entry>DDR5-6400 ECC RDIMM (16 GB, 32 GB, 64 GB, or 128 GB)</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>DIMM count</entry><?Pub Caret -1?>
<entry>1, 2, 4, or 8</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry>Maximum capacity</entry>
<entry>Up to 1 TB (8 × 128 GB)</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table></p>
<section><title>Configuration rules</title><p><ul>
<li><p>Systems configured with Intel Xeon 638, 636, or 634 processors
support a maximum of four 128 GB DDR5-6400 ECC RDIMM modules per system.</p></li>
<li><p>Multiple modules in one system must be identical in type and
capacity.</p></li>
<li><p>Memory modules must be installed in the following order: DIMM
3, 8, 1, 6, 4, 5, 2, and 7.</p></li>
</ul></p></section>
</body>
